# Varve search-ignore policy (repository context hygiene).
#
# .ignore is the enforced ignore file for ripgrep and fd. This repository is
# large: the local Tauri build tree reaches ~9.9 GB, node_modules ~1.5 GB, and
# generated review captures add hundreds of MB. Search tools that walk those
# trees waste agent tokens and time on content that is not source.
#
# .dshignore and .opencodeignore contain the same rules for agent harnesses
# that look for their own convention filename. Keep all three files identical.
#
# Rules are gitignore-style: one pattern per line, "#" starts a comment,
# "dir/" matches a directory at any depth, "!" re-includes a later pattern.
# These files affect SEARCH only. .gitignore still governs commits; lockfiles
# and the bundled ONNX models below remain tracked for reproducibility.

# --- Package installs ---
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# --- Rust build output (native engine / Tauri) ---
# apps/desktop/src-tauri/target is ~9.9 GB after a release build.
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target/
**/target/

# --- JS/TS build, cache and coverage output ---
dist/
build/
.next/
.astro/
coverage/
.vitest-cache/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Test and review artifacts ---
playwright-report/
test-results/
test-results-*/
reports/
artifacts/
.flatpak-builder/

# --- Desktop build output copied into source trees ---
apps/desktop/dist-try/
apps/desktop/public/wasm/
apps/desktop/public/ort-wasm/
apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/
apps/desktop/src-tauri/onnxruntime-libs

# --- Local git worktrees (parallel-agent checkouts) ---
# .worktrees/ holds independent checkouts used for parallel work; a single
# stale checkout duplicates source and carries its own build output. .gitignore
# also excludes it, but this rule keeps search behavior independent of VCS
# configuration and of hidden-directory handling.
.worktrees/

# --- Local agent pipeline state (generated, untracked) ---
# Coordination plans/research/evidence written by agent sessions, not source.
.pipeline/

# --- Lockfiles (tracked intentionally for reproducible installs; never search them) ---
Cargo.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json
*.lock
uv.lock

# --- Binary / generated media ---
*.wasm
*.onnx
*.zip

# --- Generated review captures and evidence ---
docs/screenshots/
docs/**/artifacts/

# --- Vendored third-party source (486 MB, 151 tracked files) ---
# Not Varve source. Search only when patching a vendored crate: pass the exact
# path or use --no-ignore for a deliberate vendor-wide search.
vendor/

# --- SVG assets ---
# Generated artwork and reference fixtures, not searchable source. The shared
# brand/icon sources under packages/ui/src/icons stay searchable because
# components reference them by name.
*.svg
!packages/ui/src/icons/*.svg
